(Discrepancy 1 (ENV) — RESOLVED (vox #58), re-recorded 2026-08-22
 against vox 0.4.9. Used to be: declaring a buffer DIRECTLY from an
 `environment's <property>` expression (`"NAME"`, `first`, or `last`
 all reproduced) never copied the string's bytes in — content printed
 empty, `'s size` was -1, and `'s empty` reported FALSE despite the
 content being empty. Going through an intermediate `text` variable
 first worked correctly even on 0.4.8 (see ENV-03.vox), which is what
 made this a copy-path bug rather than a read-path one. D1b.vox showed
 the identical failure on `arguments's first`.
 Now: the buffer-direct form and the text-then-buffer form agree, which
 is the same "agreement" oracle this ledger's other rows use — no raw
 host PATH content is printed or asserted against a fixed value, per
 this project's rule against checking host state into a file
 (gen_misc.vox:39-101's incident); only sizes and a match verdict.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   direct and indirect sizes agree: yes
   direct buffer is empty: no
   direct buffer capacity is non-negative: yes
)
a buffer called pathbuf is environment's "PATH".
a text called pathtext is environment's "PATH".
a buffer called pathbuf2 is pathtext.
If pathbuf's size is equal to pathbuf2's size then, print "direct and indirect sizes agree: yes". Otherwise, print "direct and indirect sizes agree: no".
If pathbuf's empty then, print "direct buffer is empty: yes". Otherwise, print "direct buffer is empty: no".
If pathbuf's capacity is greater than or equal to 0 then, print "direct buffer capacity is non-negative: yes". Otherwise, print "direct buffer capacity is non-negative: no".
